WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:02.480
So, hey.

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.910
Who do you think is the 
cutest girl in our class?

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:06.860
Uh...

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.260
How about Amakusa?

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.540
Ah, well, you always did 
like the pretty girls.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.500
Huh? It's not like that. What?

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.360
What about you, Kai?

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.530
Huh? What?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.750
Jeez, do you ever listen?

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.630
By the way, Amakusa's big bro 
came to the cultural festival.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.020
Oh, he did?

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.340
He looked just like Amakusa. 
He was super hot.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.420
That's just a roundabout way 
of saying that Amakusa is hot.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.840
Huh? It's not like that. What?

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.260
Hey, is Amakusa's brother tall, 
with his hair parted mostly to one side?

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.180
Yeah, that's him.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.430
<b>Smack</b>

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:43.990
Kai!

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.190
<b>Can't express
the pain with words</b>

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.190
Oh, my gosh! I'm so sorry!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.940
<b>The culprit</b>

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.940
Are you all right?

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.530
I'm so sorry! Are you hurt?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.220
Wait, Tamaru-kun, are you okay? 
Say something, please.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.440
I'm fine. Here.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.820
Thanks.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.780
That was some changeup.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.780
I'm sorry.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.410
Nice, Ichika.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.210
There's nothing nice about that at all!

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.120
A critical right to his noggin!

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.960
<b>Cackle                  Cackle</b>

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.340
Damn, Arima!

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.960
<b>Stab
Stab
Stab</b>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.520
It's not that funny.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.550
Hey, ow! Stop hitting my shin!

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.010
Koikimo

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.020
Episode 3

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.020
"You're Just Messing With Me"

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.080
Tamaru-kun.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.320
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.090
Is your forehead okay?

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.440
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.570
F
o
r
w
a
r
d

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.570
Tamaru-kun, that's...

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.810
Huh? What?

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.590
S-Sorry. It's just that 
I love that series, too.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.160
The anime's airing now, you know?

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.970
I started with the anime, but lately, 
I've been collecting the original series.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.380
And I've been enjoying that a lot, too!

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.010
I have the full set of the original series.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.160
What? That's amazing! 
There are so many volumes.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.880
I still only have up to volume 3.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:27.600
Wanna borrow mine?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.520
Really?!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.670
<i>Wow, she's really interested.</i>

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.840
Okay, I'll bring them tomorrow.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.440
Thank you!

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.200
Want to read the Gaiden series, too?

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.570
Yeah, I do!

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:38.730
Okay, I'll look for them.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.540
Thank you so much!

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.310
<i>Yes? Hello?</i>

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.800
Hello?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.670
<i>Oh, sorry.</i>

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.960
You usually don't answer until 
it rings at least ten times,

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.550
so I was a bit surprised.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.510
<i>Am I not allowed to answer immediately?</i>

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.560
Of course you can! It makes me very happy.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.780
<i>I think I'll be extra 
productive at work tomorrow.</i>

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.050
Please just be productive 
at work on the regular.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.160
Ichika-san, are you outside right now?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.940
<i>Huh? Yes, I am.</i>

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.830
<i>Are you walking home by yourself?</i>

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.380
Uh... yes.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.980
<i>You shouldn't be walking around 
alone this late at night.</i>

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:32.330
I'm a bit more concerned that you 
call me at this hour every night.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.680
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:35.470
Huh?

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.450
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.100
Why do you ask?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.120
<i>Just curious.</i>

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:44.010
I'm in front of the convenience 
store in Sakuramachi.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.130
<i>Sakuramachi...</i>

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.540
Excellent. You're nearby.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.890
Please stay right there. 
I'll be there in about five minutes.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:51.700
Huh?!

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.360
<i>If you move away from there, I'll be 
visiting your house tomorrow morning</i>

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.650
<i>wearing a white tuxedo, 
with a bouquet of roses in hand.</i>

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.710
Wait, what? Hello?

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.010
<i>It's probably quicker 
to run than grab a taxi.</i>

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:19.050
<i>I never thought I'd end up 
running like this for anyone.</i>

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.300
<i>He's not answering my calls. 
I guess I'll just have to wait. Ugh.</i>

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:35.710
Ichika-san!

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.230
Thank goodness. You waited for me.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.770
Y-You actually showed up. 
And... wait, you ran here?

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.010
Yes. I ran as fast as I could.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.240
You answered my call immediately because 
you were scared to walk alone at night, right?

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.700
N-No! I just felt like answering early.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:57.510
Of course.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.340
And you showed up in three minutes...

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:07.590
<b>Beam              ing</b>

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.670
I ran as fast as I could. 
Now, please allow me to walk you home.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.160
<i>Ugh, why? This sucks...</i>

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.890
<i>Why do I feel at ease now?</i>

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.220
Arima?

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:18.970
Tamaru-kun?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.190
What a coincidence.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.560
I live right around the corner.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.480
Evening.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.570
Evening.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.570
So, Ichika-chan, who might this be?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.600
Oh, this is my classmate, Tamaru Kai-kun.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.450
Ah, so he's a classmate.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.760
And, uh, Tamaru-kun, this is...

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.460
I so
don't
want to
introduce
him...

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.710
Amakusa's big brother, right?

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.670
You know who I am?

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.990
I saw you at the cultural festival,

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.650
and my friend told me that
you were Amakusa's brother.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.800
Ah, I see.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:59.060
Tamaru-kun, I hope you continue to get 
along with my sister as classmates.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.570
Uh, sure.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.220
Oh, by the way, Arima. I'll bring you 
the Gaiden from that series tomorrow.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.570
Really? Thanks!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.450
I've been wanting to read it,

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.210
considering where the series ended before it.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.840
Well, I'm going in the store now.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.960
Okay. I'll see you at school tomorrow.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:22.330
Tamaru-kun.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.290
Yes?

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:29.920
I hope you continue to get along 
with Ichika-san <i>as classmates</i>.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.430
Okay, let's go, Ichika-san.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.000
Huh? Okay.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.370
Let's take the long way back.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.910
What? No.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.900
I just broke out in a cold sweat...

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.990
Oh, yeah.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.990
Here, you can have this.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:58.480
I think I remember you drinking black 
coffee when we were at that café.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.000
Th-Thank you so much!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.620
I will worship this every day! 
Oh, no! Where should I place it, though?

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.130
Please, just drink it right now.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.110
<b>Moved</b>

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.110
Put yourself in that poor coffee's shoes.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:12.130
You remembered that I drank black coffee.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:16.770
By the way, you were drinking 
a medium iced tea then.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.390
Why would you remember the size?

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:24.740
I even remember all of the problems 
you were trying to solve back then.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:28.360
I want to make sure I can help you with the 
subjects you struggle with at any time.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.360
Ugh...

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.840
Your memory is way too good.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:38.370
<i>Tamaru Kai, huh?</i>

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.180
<i>I guess I'll get info from Rio when I get home.</i>

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.210
Arima.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.330
Here you go.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:52.920
The book I mentioned yesterday.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.980
Oh, thank you!

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:59.550
I'm so happy! Oh, man, 
I have a test coming up, though!

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.640
I might not be able to 
stop reading once I start.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.780
Say...

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.130
Hm? What is it?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.240
Are you going out with 
Amakusa's older brother?

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.410
<b>Camera 1</b>

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:19.780
m 0 0 l 138 0 l 138 50 l 0 50

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Camera 2</b>

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.780
<b>Camera 3</b>

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.780
Wha...

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.710
What?! Wait, why?! Huh? What? Why?!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.180
<b>Panic</b>

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.290
Wh-Wh-Why, though?! Huh? What?!

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.290
Well, at the cultural festival...

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.630
Did you think I wouldn't notice?!

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.590
<i>Wait, was that Arima?!</i>

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.170
My body just reacted on its own.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.850
<i>That's Arima and...</i>

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.110
How were you going to explain this 
to my friends if they saw you?!

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.350
<i>Who is that guy?</i>

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.840
Why are you smirking?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.350
I saw you two

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:48.560
hugging in the stairwell, so...

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.610
<i>He saw us!</i>

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.130
This
is
the
worst

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.110
N-No! We absolutely are not dating!

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.510
It's just that Ryo-san...

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:59.280
Rio's older brother... caught me when 
I was about to fall down the stairs.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.700
We weren't actually hugging!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.120
It was a total coincidence!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.640
We absolutely are not going out!

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.960
O-Okay, I got it.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.480
Oh, sorry...

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.040
I'm sorry I had the wrong idea.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.110
No, I'm sorry for yelling.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.470
I never knew you could yell 
like that. That was unexpected.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:25.000
Really? I do get pretty loud 
and say witty things fairly often.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.650
<i>Like when it has to do with 
Ryo-san or I'm watching anime...</i>

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.040
So about Amakusa's brother...

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.440
I'm not sure you should take him seriously.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.270
Huh?

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.650
He seemed to be messing with you.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.700
That startled me.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.090
Not to mention...

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:03.300
Grrrrrr

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.660
<i>It's so embarrassing knowing someone saw us.</i>

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.300
<i>And it was a guy from my class!</i>

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.530
He seemed to be messing with you.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.250
Messing with me?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.560
Er, forget I said anything.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.480
<i>Oh, right.</i>

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.720
<i>I guess that is actually a possibility.</i>

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.620
<i>Why didn't I think of that before?</i>

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:33.000
Koikimo

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Koikimo

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Forehead
is still
slightly
red

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.340
Rio, how do I solve this again?

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.050
Well—

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:43.780
Ichika-san!

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.220
You use this theorem and...

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.580
I didn't ask you, Ryo-san.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:51.360
I'm pretty sure my brother could 
teach you in better detail.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:52.390
Uh...

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:56.150
Please call me Ryo-sensei 
to your heart's content!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:59.420
What I would like to know 
the most is why you're here

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:02.450
when we're supposed to 
be studying for our test.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.780
The answer is simply because 
you're here, Ichika-san!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:07.780
Koromogawa-senpai

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.290
Oh, sorry.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.290
Koromogawa-senpai

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.770
My senpai from my club is calling me.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:12.700
I'll be back.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:13.420
Okay.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.710
Hello?

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:19.940
<i>Wait...</i>

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.060
<i>We're alone together in 
her bedroom right now!</i>

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.650
Ichika-san, were you thinking the same thi—

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:26.430
Absolutely not!

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:31.600
By the way, the boy we met at the 
convenience store... Tamaru-kun, was it?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.710
Yes?

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.660
He was rather handsome.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:39.500
Oh... Yeah, there are quite 
a few girls who say he's hot.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.440
m 0 0 l 110 0 l 110 180 l 0 180

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>*Already
got intel
on
Tamaru
from Rio</b>

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.440
Oh, I see.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.630
What do you think of him, Ichika-san?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:49.920
Me? I don't think I've ever 
looked at his face that closely,

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.010
but he's probably handsome.

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:54.080
<b>Smile...</b>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.080
I see...

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.460
Oh, for the record, how do you feel about me?

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.470
I think you're pretty well put-together. 
Only on the outside, though.

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.090
Why, thank you very much.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.000
<i>I guess he's used to hearing that.</i>

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.630
Though I believe that you're 
the most beautiful and

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.560
precious person in this world, Ichika-san.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.410
He seemed to be messing with you.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.900
Wh-Why do you always say things like that?

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:26.020
Well, it's because I love you, of cour—

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.630
You're just saying those things to get

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:31.660
a reaction out of me every time, aren't you?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:36.120
I'm younger than you, 
and I'm not used to any of this,

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.500
so you're just messing with 
me for fun, aren't you?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.140
Oh, I see...

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.810
I guess that's how I made you feel.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:58.900
But... and even I realize that it's silly,

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.400
but my feelings for you are genuine.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.490
Sorry, I'm finally off the phone.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:08.720
She ended up asking me for relationship 
advice, for some reason.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:09.410
Rio.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:13.460
I've got some work to do, 
so I'm gonna head to the office.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:17.040
It's that urgent? Okay, I guess...

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.540
Ichika-san.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.400
Good luck with your studies.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.380
Uh... thanks.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:29.220
My brother seemed to be acting a 
bit weird. Did something happen?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.720
<i>Before, he'd always smile, 
no matter what I said.</i>

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.740
<i>He's never looked like that before.</i>

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.540
Rio... I said something 
really mean to Ryo-san.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.470
<i>After that day,</i>

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:51.420
<i>Ryo-san continued to call me every day,
as if nothing had ever happened.</i>

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.070
Huh? Uh, okay.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.380
Goodnight, then.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.000
<i>Why can't I just apologize to him?</i>

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.350
<i>Hey, what's up?</i>

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:33.920
Masuda? You know how to use Photoshop, right?

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.340
I have a favor to ask.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.050
A cold?

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.620
Yeah.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.600
Got it. No worries. Just get some rest.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.260
Okay, feel better soon.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.980
Oh, are you heading out?

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.010
Didn't you say you were off today?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.990
I need to get some documents from work.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.510
You're heading out, too, aren't you?

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:56.600
Well, I was planning to, but...

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.390
Ichika

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.390
Ichika

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.390
I'm so sorry!

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.390
No worries.
Feel better soon.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:03.570
I was supposed to go out with Ichika, 
but she caught a cold and has a fever.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:04.400
What?!

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:09.800
I was thinking about visiting her. 
Did you want to come— Oh.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.150
<b>Gone</b>

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.190
Damn, he's fast.

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:16.260
I said something really mean to Ryo-san.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.970
<i>They've been awkward ever since that day,</i>

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.960
<i>so I hope this helps them work things out.</i>

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:30.380
<i>I need to make this up to Rio.</i>

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:33.790
Yes?

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.670
Ichika, were you asleep?

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:39.060
No... What's wrong?

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:42.810
An "Amakusa-san" is here to see you.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.230
Sh-Should I let them in?

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.060
Yeah, sure.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.420
<i>I guess Rio came to see me.</i>

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.240
Are you sure?

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:50.080
Yeah.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.730
You're really sure?

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.020
I said yes, jeez.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:17:00.010
<i>My mom's met Rio. What was that about?</i>

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.710
Yes? Come in.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:06.290
Pardon me! Ichika-san, are you all right?!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.540
Huh?!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.360
Well, make yourself at home, Ryo-kun.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.480
Thank you very much for 
your concern, Yuriko-san.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.050
<i>Wait... "Amakusa" was </i>that<i> Amakusa-san?!</i>

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.280
<i>Also, why are they calling 
each other by their first names?</i>

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.170
I'm sorry it's so messy.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:20.430
Oh, it's perfectly fine.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.790
I'm sorry for showing up so suddenly. 
My name is Amakusa Ryo.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.790
I'm Ichika-san's friend's older brother.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.920
m 0 0 l 365 0 l 365 45 l 0 45

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.920
They talked for about 30 minutes at the front door

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.960
Wait... Amakusa Ryo-san?

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.420
The one sending the flowers?

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:34.160
<i>I'm in my pajamas right 
now and my hair's a mess.</i>

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:37.080
I'm sorry for showing up out of the blue.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.740
How are you feeling?

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:44.150
I-I'm okay... Did Rio tell you?

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:47.210
Yes. I brought you a few things.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.610
I have a variety of cold 
medicine, cool gel sheets,

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.330
pudding, gelatin, some fruit...

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.480
Oh, and something to drink, and...

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:59.340
I appreciate it, but you 
clearly bought too much.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.800
Is something wrong?

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.800
No, no. Don't mind me.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.790
<i>As imprudent as it may sound,</i>

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:09.460
<b>Self-Restraint Switch</b>

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:09.150
<i>her jabs at me seem even sexier 
because she's weakened.</i>

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.810
<b>Self-Restraint Switch</b>

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:10.810
<i>She's so precious.</i>

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.890
Then may I have the gelatin?

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.810
Yes, of course. Here you go.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:21.400
Please don't get too close. 
I don't want you to catch my cold.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.670
I'd be more than happy to catch your cold.

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:24.840
Please don't say that.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:28.290
Actually, they say a cold heals faster
if you give it to someone else.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.390
Let me catch it!

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:31.470
Uh, what are you even saying?

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:34.680
Oh, I'm sorry. Are you all right?

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:38.640
It's good.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.680
At least you have an appetite. 
Thank goodness.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:45.730
My fever's not that high, either. 
I just have a cough.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.010
Ichika-san, that part of your room...

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:52.480
I-I didn't know what to do with them, 
so they just all ended up together.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.730
So you've put them all on display.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:56.480
Thank you so much.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:58.570
Oh, I'll take care of the trash.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.870
<i>Thank goodness... 
He's acting like he usually does.</i>

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:03.710
Um—

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:05.470
Oh, right. Before I forget...

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:06.730
Here.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.040
For Ichika-san

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.040
You've got this,
Ichika-san!

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.040
<b>Mathematics Study Guide</b>

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.500
What's this?

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:16.170
I asked Rio what might be on the test 
and made a study guide just for you.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.170
<b>Supervising Editor: Ryo</b>

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.170
<b>Cover: Masuda</b>

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.770
It's too thick to staple together...

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:19.130
Hm? It's too thick to staple together...

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.450
<i>You know how to use Photoshop, right?</i>

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.790
<i>Make me a study guide cover 
within thirty minutes.</i>

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:24.720
What?

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.470
I'm sorry... I was in a hurry, 
so it's not very well-made...

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.230
<b>Let's learn the trigonometric function formulas!</b>

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.180
But I'm hoping this will help 
you study for your test.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.870
<b>Try your best to learn this formula!</b>

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:33.980
<b>Exponential function & logarithmic function</b>

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.000
Is something the matter?

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:44.210
You always pull things off so flawlessly,

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.740
but this has such a handmade feel...

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.750
I'm sorry for laughing.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:57.750
Um...

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.470
I'm sorry for the mean things I said

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:03.330
when we were studying for 
our test the other day.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.140
Mean things?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:09.040
That didn't bother me at all.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:15.070
But... it's true that I made 
you look distraught, so...

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.480
I'm sorry.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.140
It's okay.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:28.870
So what you're saying... is that you've 
accepted my love, is that right?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.770
How did you reach that conclusion?

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.380
Well, isn't that what it means?

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:34.740
How can you possibly reach 
that misunderstanding?

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:38.000
Oh, that reminds me. 
I borrowed Masuda's camera.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:42.010
May I take a photo of you ill?

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.420
Did you honestly think I'd say yes?!

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:49.650
Now, now. You shouldn't shout. 
It'll make your cold worse.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:51.980
And whose fault is that?!

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:55.670
Oh, Ichika-san.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:58.160
We should probably swap 
out your cool gel sheet...

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:20.890
Thank you...

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:24.130
for apologizing.

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.850
<b>Mathematics Periodic Exam Answer Sheet</b>

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.850
<b>Name:   Arima Ichika</b>

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.230
No way...

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.960
Did you get a bad score?

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:37.320
No... I did really well.

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:38.660
Then what's the problem?

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:42.230
There isn't one, exactly... 
But it's somehow still upsetting.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:46.950
This happened because I used 
Ryo-san's study guide,

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.230
so I just feel... you know...

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:50.200
Huh...

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:53.700
It's a good thing, so just be happy.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:56.240
Yeah... I know, but...

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:57.880
Ichika! Rio!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.170
Hey, Satsuki. How'd you do?

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.880
<i>I need to make sure I thank him.</i>

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:09.890
Acting Section Chief Amakusa, 
did something good happen?

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:11.180
Why do you ask?

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:17.680
You'd seemed a bit down lately, 
but you seem to be in higher spirits now.

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:21.850
I guess I've got some stuff to work 
on if you're seeing through me.

00:22:21.850 --> 00:22:24.280
Don't underestimate my 
keen observation skills.

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:28.120
I'm not sure if I'd say something good 
happened. It's more of a hunch.

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:31.450
I'm sure she scored pretty well.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
"On This Holy Night"

00:23:35.990 --> 00:23:38.330
Next time, "On This Holy Night."
